    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "It's very rare that a spacious three bedroom terraced period house comes to the market situated on the main street in the town centre. While in need of modernisation, the ample space and generous accommodation of this property offers any purchaser a great opportunity to create a vibrant modern home. With many original features in place such as doors, fireplaces, stairs and ceiling cornice, this property would make a beautiful home. \r\nThis property comes with the benefit of a large rear garden which is not overlooked and off street parking to the rear. Dublin Street is within a minutes walk to the long sandy beaches and harbour area. As well as three superb beaches in the town and great walking routes, there are also numerous sports clubs and facilities including golf, Gaelic football, soccer, rowing and rugby to name just a few.\r\n\r\nBalbriggan town centre offers a host of amenities and services along with the train station that provides daily services to and from Dublin City centre and its suburbs. Balbriggan is home to the Irish Institute of Music and Song and the Lark Theatre. It is also conveniently situated near the coastal town of Skerries and a short drive to the M1 motorway providing very easy access to the city centre, Port tunnel and Dublin International Airport.  \r\nRejuvenation works around the harbour area    are almost completed, with a multi-purpose plaza to host social events and markets. The works will redefine both sides of the historic viaduct also enhancing the beach and coastline. The redevelopment will bring increased social and commercial activity to the area. With ample space and generous accommodation, this property offers any purchaser a great opportunity to settle into an idyllic seaside family home."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Hall \t\t            5.0m x 1.9m\r\nWith tiled flooring and carpeted stairs to the first floor.\r\n\r\nLiving Room\t            6.0m x 4.5m\r\nLarge bright room with wooden flooring and coving.\r\n \r\nKitchen\t\t            6.1m x 4.8m\r\nWith wall and floor units, tiled splashback, vinyl flooring, plumbed for a fridge freezer, stainless steel sink. \r\n\r\nBathroom \t            2.3m x 1.8m\r\nWith tiled floor and walls, wash hand basin and bath and shower.\r\n\r\nWC\t                         2.4m x 0.8m\r\nWith tiled floor, WC and wash hand basin.\r\n\r\nUtility Room\t           2.8m x 1.5m\r\nPlumbed for washing machine and sink.\r\n\r\nFirst Floor\r\n\r\nLanding \r\nWith carpet flooring.\r\n\r\nBathroom \t                          2.3m x 1.8m\r\nWith tiled floor and partially tiled walls around the shower, WC and a vanity unit.\r\n\r\nBedroom 1 \t\t            4.0m x 3.4m\r\nDouble bedroom with wooden flooring, built in wardrobes and a TV point. \r\n\r\nBedroom 2  \t\t            3.9m x 3.2m \r\nDouble bedroom with wooden flooring, built in wardrobe and TV point.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3  \t\t              3.6m x 3.5m \r\nDouble bedroom with carpet flooring, and built in wardrobe.\r\n\r\nGarage\t\t\t              6.0m x 3.1m\r\nWith concrete floor and a roller shutter door.  \r\n\r\nRear Garden\r\nLarge, private garden with walled boundaries and a grass area along with mature shrubs. Concrete built shed with electric points and a roller door. There is access to communal laneway to the rear of the property."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Town Centre Location \r\nPeriod property with many original features\r\nLarge rear garden with potential to extend with PP\r\nGood sized rooms\r\nDoor off sunroom to the enclosed rear garden \r\nCar parking to front\r\nOil heating"
      },
